---
title: "Phase 3: Repository Selection"
---
flowchart TD
    sub["Data Publication Workflow | Entry 3: Ready to deposit data joins here"]:::subtitle
    r10["<b>R10 (Horizontal Requirement — all phases):</b> Track provenance of all AI agent actions on data and metadata. Record all actions so they can be verified, validated and audited."]:::horizontal
    sub ~~~ r10 ~~~ entry3

    entry3(["Entry 3: Ready to deposit data — joins here"]):::entry
    phase3["PHASE 3: REPOSITORY SELECTION"]:::phase
    assumes["Assumes governance and constraints checks are met"]:::caption
    mandated{"Is a repository mandated by funder, journal or institution?"}:::decision
    usemandated["Use mandated repository"]:::step
    find["Find a suitable repository (domain-specific or generalist)<br><br><b>Guidance note:</b> The agent could suggest options — the researcher selects. The agent distinguishes commercial from open repositories, surfaces deposit fees, and connects to FAIRsharing MCP server and re3data API.<br><br><b>R1:</b> Recommend and select repositories meeting funder, journal, institutional and community requirements"]:::step
    pids{"Does the repository assign Persistent Identifiers (PIDs) automatically?"}:::decision
    auto["PID auto-assigned (skip PID step at deposit)"]:::step
    arrange["Arrange PID assignment (e.g. via DataCite)<br><br><b>Guidance note:</b> The agent could support PID arrangement. PID assignment is the responsibility of the repository, not the researcher. PIDs include Handles and other GUPRIs (Globally Unique, Persistent and Resolvable Identifiers) — not DOIs only.<br><br><b>R7:</b> Support assignment of persistent identifiers (PIDs) at point of publication"]:::step
    access["Check access options and deposit costs<br><br><b>Guidance note:</b> The agent could surface information on access options, deposit fees and costs for the selected repository."]:::step
    cert["Check repository certification e.g. CoreTrustSeal (OPTIONAL)<br><br><b>Guidance note:</b> Free evaluation options are available via FAIRsharing and EDEN/FIDELIS for assessing repository quality. The agent should not weight paid certification more highly than free options."]:::optional
    next["→ Continues to Phase 4: Data Preparation and Metadata Creation (see next page)"]:::link

    entry3 --> phase3
    phase3 ~~~ assumes
    assumes --> mandated
    mandated -- YES --> usemandated
    mandated -- NO --> find
    usemandated --> pids
    find --> pids
    pids -- YES --> auto
    pids -- NO --> arrange
    auto --> access
    arrange --> access
    access ~~~ cert
    cert --> next

